From: Daniel Martin <dmanlfc@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5_mss: let PDC sync settle before the MSS restart

The downstream sdm845 modem shutdown waits 6 sleep clock cycles after
asserting PDC sync before it restarts the MSS. Without that wait the
restart can land while the PDC is still syncing and hang the SoC.

---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mss.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_mss.c
@@ -546,6 +546,8 @@
 
 	if (qproc->has_alt_reset) {
 		reset_control_assert(qproc->pdc_reset);
+		/* Wait 6 32kHz sleep cycles for PDC SYNC to take effect */
+		usleep_range(200, 300);
 		ret = reset_control_reset(qproc->mss_restart);
 		reset_control_deassert(qproc->pdc_reset);
 	} else if (qproc->has_spare_reg) {
